.SH NAME
.PP
auto-set-umask - Change default umask for all users

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-set-umask umask
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
umask   The new umask in octal
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-set-umask
command changes the default umask for all users.  This is typically
desirable on shared systems, such as HPC clusters, in order to
keep files private from other users by default.  The default
umask is commonly 022, which enables group and other read permissions
by default.  A umask of 027 is more appropriate where security
matters, allowing group read access, but denying other access.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-set-umask 027
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8), umask(*)

